## Context

Arena run 2026-10-29, one Opus team lead, 6 merges, 1.33 of 5 USD, zero stalls, zero leftover trees; what nearly failed was agent context (213K and 192K of about 236K).

## Scope

skills/raid/references/autonomous-brief.md, cited by raid and team-lead:

1. the goal as an observable outcome;
2. a hard USD cap that includes child spend, with a ledger that shows its arithmetic;
3. waves with roar between them and a lair at the end of the day;
4. watchdogs over executors as well as runs, plus the classifier-denial rule: rewrite to match an allow rule literally (git -C, no cd prefix), or log it and move on, never retry verbatim;
5. a named advisor model for calls outside a ticket's scope;
6. the author's by-right decisions queued, one line each with a default;
7. a context rule: at about 75% of the ceiling, write a handoff note, and give bounded risky windows to a fresh agent;
8. sitreps from side effects (git log, ps, health endpoints), never from transcripts;
9. a broadcast to every agent before taking a shared resource (GPU, production).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The reference exists and is cited by raid and team-lead.
- [ ] One run reports against it.
- [ ] The denial rule is added to rules/claude-code.md § Allow rules.
